{"title":"2009 Grade 8 CEMC Gauss Problems/Problem 8","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_Grade_8_CEMC_Gauss_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The number of faces (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />), vertices (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/d/12d58aa29201da09d8e620f8698e3a37547f6b4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />), and edges (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />) of a polyhedron are related by the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/2/3626911d56c25078424fed594319a776cfa99ad3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F + V - E = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"123\" height=\"16\" />. If a polyhedron has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> faces and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> vertices, how many edges does it have?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/2/16279eab0db3c9030a443bb82c1a476317ddf216.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 12 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 14 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 16 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 18 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"433\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_Grade_8_CEMC_Gauss_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can use the equation provided in the problem, and plug in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/d/12d58aa29201da09d8e620f8698e3a37547f6b4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/d/f1dd6936bf5cda6fb0f95a332fc3bc12be0f95c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 + 8 - E = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"112\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>We can combine <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/a/8fa85dbbef5d5cb5964f6502e7ad09d56af07a7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14 - E = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"90\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Adding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to both sides, we get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/7/9f7b8fcc9d6cc2fd52d1ae2f6c13a6e2745a3364.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E + 2 = 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"90\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Subtracting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> from both sides of the equation, we get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/b/67b87befbc63b258f30c1afd2e4a497959dec2ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E = \\boxed {\\textbf {(A) } 12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"106\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_Grade_8_CEMC_Gauss_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can remember that a rectangular prism has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> faces, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> vertices, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/b/c1b4ff8a36fb4c24cc6bf9a491edcc0e51a95cee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(A) } 12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"67\" height=\"30\" /> edges, without doing any calculation.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017221837\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.012 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.021 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 112/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3971/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:32527:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017221837 and revision id 251528. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}